#   Slack; Flip, a Church Boolean, true makes the near miss. Sized by a probe of
#   2026-09-30 (CPUs 0-5, 1024 MB stack and table, the machine shared),
#   each reading equal to its snapshot: tabling(weak_head) reads 24 bits
#   (the fewest 7) in 509 ms, 33 bits (11) in 16595 ms and 40 bits (13) in
#   827 ms (the cost depends on how the dictionary's words overlap, not on
#   the length alone), and is stopped at 60 s on 99 bits (33) and 240 bits
#   (74); 48 bits (16) were stopped too. The traps read nothing, in 8999 ms
#   (one short) and 298 ms (flipped). The native reference
#   fewest_segments/3 answers every point in 9 ms or less.
#
